{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02670",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 3.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.95,
      "end_seconds": 5.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Hello, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.95,
      "end_seconds": 9.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.11,
      "end_seconds": 21.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a growing red ring on my thigh. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.68,
      "end_seconds": 25.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.41,
      "end_seconds": 32.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Oh, around ten days... no wait, it's more like three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.7,
      "end_seconds": 39.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.5,
      "end_seconds": 51.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "A mild headache goes along with it, most of the time. With mild headache, mostly moderate. It happens on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.09,
      "end_seconds": 67.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "So, have you had any stiff neck, facial weakness, joint swelling or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.59,
      "end_seconds": 73.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "No, you know, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.53,
      "end_seconds": 77.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.3,
      "end_seconds": 82.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.41,
      "end_seconds": 86.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.59,
      "end_seconds": 99.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "An enlarged prostate, for about a year. I did try to ignore it for a while. I've got epilepsy. Yes, an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.4,
      "end_seconds": 111.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "Right, right. Yes, an enlarged prostate is known to us, good to have that clear. Alright, is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.09,
      "end_seconds": 117.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Let me think, my grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.83,
      "end_seconds": 137.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.22,
      "end_seconds": 141.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.72,
      "end_seconds": 145.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.32,
      "end_seconds": 150.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Tamsulosin, at night for the prostate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.97,
      "end_seconds": 154.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.53,
      "end_seconds": 173.76,
      "duration_seconds": 18.23,
      "text": "0.4 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. Carbamazepine. I take it 200 milligrams, twice a day for the seizures. I take thyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.4,
      "end_seconds": 177.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.87,
      "end_seconds": 189.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.79,
      "end_seconds": 193.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.34,
      "end_seconds": 201.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Yes, I had a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 202.92,
      "end_seconds": 212.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 112 over 81, temp 36.8 degrees, respiratory rate 14. Pulse 65, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.1,
      "end_seconds": 214.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.98,
      "end_seconds": 219.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.07,
      "end_seconds": 235.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.01,
      "end_seconds": 239.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.55,
      "end_seconds": 252.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "There is an expanding ring-shaped red patch, about eight centimetres across, on the thigh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.33,
      "end_seconds": 264.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is early Lyme disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.71,
      "end_seconds": 268.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.49,
      "end_seconds": 291.62,
      "duration_seconds": 21.13,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like early Lyme disease. I'll start you on doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, twenty-one days. You take it by mouth. That should help with early Lyme disease. Take the doxycycline with food and avoid strong sun."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.2,
      "end_seconds": 304.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Right, right. Please come and see me in three weeks. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.27,
      "end_seconds": 314.27,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "So, I take the doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day and come back in three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.66,
      "end_seconds": 320.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.22,
      "end_seconds": 325.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.44,
      "end_seconds": 328.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}